WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:44.773
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:45.043 --> 01:46.511
Thanks for the food.

3
01:46.578 --> 01:47.979
Thank you so much.

4
01:48.046 --> 01:50.281
NOTICE OF CLOSURE

5
01:50.348 --> 01:56.187
CLOSING DUE TO ECONOMIC CIRCUMSTANCES. THANKS FOR 20 YEARS OF SMILES.

6
01:56.754 --> 01:57.922
How much did you make this month?

7
02:00.225 --> 02:01.292
Pennies.

8
02:01.359 --> 02:02.493
And you?

9
02:03.861 --> 02:04.729
Dead zero.

10
02:06.264 --> 02:08.700
Do you know what young people earn now?

11
02:08.766 --> 02:12.670
A median of 2.5 million yen per year, about 150,000 yen a month after tax.

12
02:13.171 --> 02:15.707
-No wonder they can't save. -There's no dream in it.

13
02:15.773 --> 02:18.610
-None. -There's no money to steal.

14
02:18.676 --> 02:21.446
-Here you go. -Momo!

15
02:22.146 --> 02:23.381
Are you really closing the shop?

16
02:23.448 --> 02:25.917
I must get out before I fall into debt.

17
02:26.584 --> 02:28.920
-Want me to lend you some money? -Me too.

18
02:28.987 --> 02:34.459
What are you saying? You don't have money either.

19
02:34.525 --> 02:37.962
You just drift around with no steady job. I'll clear these plates.

20
02:38.029 --> 02:39.697
-Momo! -Coming.

21
02:41.099 --> 02:45.236
-Should we have told her our real job? -No way. She would faint from shock.

22
02:46.537 --> 02:48.840
Another place to relax is disappearing.

23
02:48.906 --> 02:50.541
We might be next.

24
02:50.608 --> 02:53.745
We're alive, but we are the walking dead.

25
02:53.811 --> 02:57.015
-You should be fined for your dark poetry! -It's a life-or-death problem.

26
02:57.081 --> 03:00.051
No house has money. There's no money to steal.

27
03:00.118 --> 03:02.153
True. Makes our job a bit pointless.

28
03:02.220 --> 03:05.990
"Being a thief has meaning too." I bet normal folks wouldn't want to hear that.

29
03:07.425 --> 03:11.829
We aren't thieves. We are great thieves. You always say it, Rui.

30
03:12.397 --> 03:17.535
Thieves are small-time, going after pennies or groceries.

31
03:17.602 --> 03:23.207
Meanwhile, great thieves are mysterious, gallant, and go after treasure!

32
03:23.274 --> 03:25.176
Then, same goes for great thieves.

33
03:25.243 --> 03:27.078
Oh, right. Last month…

34
03:27.945 --> 03:32.216
I went to Mr. Kanaizumi's mansion, the one I used to go to regularly.

35
03:32.283 --> 03:34.352
-That high-end neighborhood? -Yes.

36
03:34.419 --> 03:36.788
For five years, I've been taking from his savings.

37
03:36.854 --> 03:38.189
Is that what you call "great"?

38
03:40.024 --> 03:42.460
I'm just a thief when I have no choice.

39
03:42.527 --> 03:44.696
Only when I needed cash! Anyway!

40
03:44.762 --> 03:46.130
Last month, when I went there,

41
03:47.532 --> 03:49.100
Mr. Kanaizumi was dead.

42
03:51.169 --> 03:55.907
I found him on Wednesday, and he had died on Monday, so two days.

43
03:56.741 --> 04:00.178
The next day, Thursday, the housekeepers would come to clean the bath.

44
04:00.244 --> 04:02.780
-So I just left him there. -Oh my.

45
04:03.981 --> 04:06.117
He really helped me out a lot.

46
04:07.018 --> 04:08.886
So I stayed with him until night.

47
04:10.388 --> 04:13.324
I don't know if he wanted me there.

48
04:16.160 --> 04:17.362
That man…

49
04:18.362 --> 04:20.631
He was probably lonely all his life.

50
04:25.336 --> 04:26.671
I wish

51
04:27.438 --> 04:29.741
I had been your friend.

52
04:30.575 --> 04:32.343
I wish I had been your daughter.

53
04:35.146 --> 04:39.717
"But I'm a thief. Sorry." I thought.

54
04:41.552 --> 04:43.554
And the savings? You took all of it?

55
04:44.555 --> 04:48.059
I felt sad, so I just left the house without taking anything…

56
04:48.126 --> 04:49.394
-Are you stupid? -Yes, I am.

57
04:49.460 --> 04:52.163
-What a waste. -Why am I even alive?

58
04:52.230 --> 04:54.265
Hey, a fine for dark poetry.

59
04:54.332 --> 04:59.771
I wonder if I will ever find a big treasure, some really big money…

60
04:59.837 --> 05:02.473
Something that makes my heart race.

61
05:02.540 --> 05:06.978
In the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office, there is a big safe.

62
05:07.044 --> 05:09.180
It's full of money.

63
05:09.747 --> 05:15.987
It's stuffed with bundles of cash, and it's always refilled right away.

64
05:16.053 --> 05:21.159
The Finance Ministry delivers the bundles. It's the Cabinet's secret stash.

65
05:21.225 --> 05:24.395
Its official name is the Cabinet Secretariat Reward Funds.

66
05:24.462 --> 05:28.866
It's used to buy top-secret info, both at home and abroad.

67
05:28.933 --> 05:31.469
So no receipts are needed,

68
05:31.536 --> 05:34.639
and they don't have to report how it was used.

69
05:34.705 --> 05:39.510
So they exploit it and use the nation's money for their own party!

70
05:39.577 --> 05:41.813
The nation's money!

71
05:41.879 --> 05:46.551
It all comes from taxes. The people's sweat and blood!

72
05:46.617 --> 05:49.120
Is that even okay?

73
05:49.687 --> 05:51.923
The system is broken!

74
05:54.592 --> 05:56.327
I found my treasure!

75
05:59.096 --> 06:02.934
It's the Seika era, in the democratic country of Nipponia.

76
06:03.668 --> 06:07.038
A huge ruling party has held power for a long time.

77
06:07.772 --> 06:11.676
This once-rich country is now on the edge of a cliff.

78
06:11.742 --> 06:13.911
The gap between rich and poor keeps growing.

79
06:13.978 --> 06:16.214
Both blue-collar workers and yakuza have no money.

80
06:16.914 --> 06:23.654
In Nagatanicho, the center of this nation, a great thief has landed.

81
06:23.721 --> 06:26.157
Her surname is Kisaragi, her given name is Yayoi.

82
06:26.224 --> 06:30.428
What she will steal is the dark money of politicians!

83
06:31.295 --> 06:32.830
PoliticaLupin!

84
06:47.912 --> 06:49.614
Don't you find it strange?

85
06:49.680 --> 06:52.183
Eel is at risk of extinction,

86
06:52.250 --> 06:54.752
yet there's grilled eel here every day.

87
06:54.819 --> 06:56.420
What is wrong with this country?

88
06:56.487 --> 06:59.156
I'll have sushi. Northern-style seafood bowl.

89
07:00.391 --> 07:02.360
It's cheaper than eel.

90
07:02.426 --> 07:05.296
It's not about the price. Try being more critical.

91
07:07.064 --> 07:08.533
What do you do every day?

92
07:09.100 --> 07:10.735
Your sister is worried.

93
07:12.336 --> 07:14.972
Why not work for me as a secretary?

94
07:16.707 --> 07:18.442
What, work under you, Masakado?

95
07:18.509 --> 07:20.511
Call me "Mr. Natsume." Don't call me by name.

96
07:20.578 --> 07:22.213
You keep nagging me every day.

97
07:22.280 --> 07:23.781
You make me say it.

98
07:23.848 --> 07:24.682
The salary?

99
07:24.749 --> 07:27.919
A starting private secretary gets 180,000 yen after tax.

100
07:27.985 --> 07:29.320
Pretty good.

101
07:29.387 --> 07:35.126
Good? Back then, I used to earn 1.5 times this.

102
07:36.527 --> 07:39.497
-So no receipts are needed… -She's spouting nonsense again.

103
07:40.398 --> 07:42.233
Someone shut her up.

104
07:42.733 --> 07:44.969
You can't say stuff like this.

105
07:45.036 --> 07:46.070
Why say that stuff?

106
07:46.137 --> 07:48.639
Which TV station thinks this is funny?

107
07:48.706 --> 07:50.975
No need to go and expose things.

108
07:51.042 --> 07:54.145
It all comes from taxes. The people's sweat and blood!

109
07:54.211 --> 07:56.113
-What a pain. -Sounds like bad news.

110
07:57.014 --> 07:58.816
-Will it affect your work? -A little.

111
07:59.417 --> 08:00.818
Isn't it a scandal?

112
08:01.619 --> 08:04.689
Not now. Even if that kind of thing slips out, no one cares.

113
08:04.755 --> 08:05.523
Why?

114
08:05.590 --> 08:07.458
The media doesn't chase it.

115
08:07.525 --> 08:09.860
If they don't chase it, there are no follow-ups.

116
08:09.927 --> 08:12.229
With no follow-ups, people forget.

117
08:12.296 --> 08:13.898
It will stay on the Internet.

118
08:13.965 --> 08:18.536
Even if it does, most voters aren't interested in politics.

119
08:18.603 --> 08:21.872
They don't even talk about it, so it's fine.

120
08:34.986 --> 08:36.954
Oh, this is cute. Shall we pick this?

121
08:37.521 --> 08:39.056
-Okay. -I want this one!

122
08:39.123 --> 08:40.324
Really? I don't know…

123
08:54.238 --> 08:55.806
Are you Mr. Paolo?

124
08:57.008 --> 08:57.908
Here.

125
09:01.412 --> 09:02.880
-You don't want it? -I do.

126
09:10.087 --> 09:11.322
What do you want to know?

127
09:12.023 --> 09:14.859
Not many companies have cash to steal from nowadays.

128
09:15.493 --> 09:19.797
I need information from an informant who knows lots about politics.

129
09:19.864 --> 09:22.800
I heard from a friend of a friend

130
09:23.567 --> 09:26.103
that you know such informants.

131
09:27.138 --> 09:28.606
Do you read newspapers?

132
09:30.074 --> 09:31.475
Only the local news, sometimes.

133
09:32.043 --> 09:34.311
-Politics? -I plan to study it.

134
09:35.813 --> 09:37.348
What do you plan to do at that level?

135
09:37.948 --> 09:39.517
I'll steal the Cabinet secret funds.

136
09:40.851 --> 09:41.752
What?

137
09:43.220 --> 09:48.859
In the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office, there is a safe with endless cash in it.

138
09:48.926 --> 09:51.862
The safe of my dreams.

139
09:52.530 --> 09:55.299
It makes my heart race.

140
09:56.367 --> 09:58.669
It really motivates me.

141
09:59.937 --> 10:03.307
You, are you out of your mind?

142
10:04.008 --> 10:07.211
The office is inside the Prime Minister's residence,

143
10:07.278 --> 10:09.880
the second most guarded place in Nipponia.

144
10:09.947 --> 10:10.781
It's impossible.

145
10:11.348 --> 10:14.952
I'm actually a genius. Do you know the conditions that make a genius?

146
10:16.654 --> 10:20.024
Focus, playfulness, and…

147
10:20.891 --> 10:22.326
a drop of madness.

148
10:25.362 --> 10:27.098
Do you know any politics-savvy informants?

149
10:29.900 --> 10:32.970
Who can even enter the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office?

150
10:34.672 --> 10:37.775
-Cabinet ministers? Diet members? -Correct.

151
10:37.842 --> 10:40.411
If you want to steal money, become a Diet member.

152
10:40.978 --> 10:41.812
Listen up.

153
10:42.780 --> 10:45.316
The House of Representatives will be dissolved soon.

154
10:45.382 --> 10:46.650
A general election will begin.

155
10:47.485 --> 10:51.055
Any citizen aged 25 or over can run.

156
10:51.889 --> 10:55.760
If you win and become a member, I'll introduce an informant.

157
10:57.261 --> 10:59.830
Female politicians actually do pretty well.

158
10:59.897 --> 11:03.033
If you get fans, you get a lot of support, like an idol.

159
11:03.100 --> 11:04.602
You're cute too,

160
11:05.402 --> 11:06.737
so I think you can do it.

161
11:19.083 --> 11:22.052
-Cheers! -Cheers.

162
11:22.119 --> 11:24.155
What? I don't know…

163
11:24.221 --> 11:25.589
I have small eyes.

164
11:25.656 --> 11:27.825
I eat too much.

165
11:27.892 --> 11:29.126
-I get it! -I wonder…

166
11:29.193 --> 11:31.228
I think I lack self-confidence?

167
11:31.295 --> 11:32.129
Yeah…

168
11:32.196 --> 11:38.402
Hey, those aren't flaws. They are all your strengths.

169
11:38.469 --> 11:39.503
-What? -What?

170
11:39.570 --> 11:45.976
Small eyes are cool! You can also change them with makeup. I'm jealous.

171
11:46.043 --> 11:48.379
-Well, true. -Eating a lot means you're healthy.

172
11:48.445 --> 11:50.848
You would survive longest on a deserted island.

173
11:50.915 --> 11:52.082
I see!

174
11:52.149 --> 11:55.419
Not having confidence just means you have room to grow.

175
11:55.486 --> 11:57.154
You're already wonderful,

176
11:57.221 --> 11:59.023
but with a bit more confidence,

177
11:59.089 --> 12:00.724
you'll be even better.

178
12:00.791 --> 12:02.059
You'll only get better.

179
12:02.126 --> 12:03.060
I see…

180
12:03.127 --> 12:06.130
All these worries of yours are because of summer.

181
12:06.197 --> 12:08.866
Everything is because of summer.

182
12:08.933 --> 12:10.701
-Because of summer? -Because of summer?

183
12:10.768 --> 12:13.137
-Summer's at fault? Why? -Right?

184
12:13.204 --> 12:15.039
Yeah, it's summer's fault.

185
12:15.105 --> 12:18.709
-All right! Here's to summer! -To summer!

186
12:18.776 --> 12:19.877
Oh, I have to go.

187
12:19.944 --> 12:21.445
-Okay. -Okay.

188
12:23.614 --> 12:24.782
Should we go already?

189
12:25.649 --> 12:28.586
-Who is that girl? -Huh? Isn't she your friend, Yuka?

190
12:28.652 --> 12:31.956
-I don't know her. -We're out. One more bottle.

191
12:32.022 --> 12:34.458
Sorry, I have to go to work now.

192
12:34.525 --> 12:36.393
-I have to go. -Thanks for the drinks!

193
12:36.460 --> 12:40.130
-Thanks for the drinks. -Thank you.

194
12:42.299 --> 12:43.634
Bye…

195
12:52.610 --> 12:55.479
-Thank you. -Thank you.

196
12:55.546 --> 12:56.513
Yay!

197
12:59.483 --> 13:00.317
Hey.

198
13:00.384 --> 13:02.253
Sorry, I missed the train! How are things?

199
13:02.319 --> 13:04.722
Perfect. I saved you a spot.

200
13:04.788 --> 13:05.623
Here.

201
13:12.129 --> 13:13.464
Sorry I'm late…

202
13:17.134 --> 13:20.404
My friend called me here. This girl.

203
13:23.240 --> 13:26.076
-She was here earlier. -Wait, are you Miyabi?

204
13:26.143 --> 13:27.945
It's you! Long time no see!

205
13:28.512 --> 13:31.181
I'm Yayoi. Don't you remember me?

206
13:32.549 --> 13:35.486
Guess not. You were drunk after all.

207
13:37.888 --> 13:40.691
Miyabi Kobayakawa, 29, unemployed.

208
13:41.392 --> 13:44.828
Her mother died of illness, and she was raised by her grandmother.

209
13:45.763 --> 13:48.399
Her father is Shiro Kobayakawa, ex-Prime Minister.

210
13:49.400 --> 13:53.437
He served several terms and is now vice president of the ruling Kokuji Party.

211
13:54.004 --> 13:57.574
The Kobayakawas are a glamorous political family.

212
13:58.142 --> 14:01.679
But the daughter, Miyabi, only ever attracts bad rumors.

213
14:01.745 --> 14:05.649
A typical silly rich girl with too much money and time.

214
14:06.383 --> 14:10.020
Now, every time she goes out at night,

215
14:10.087 --> 14:13.991
"bodyguard" watchers follow her to make sure she doesn't go wild.

216
14:14.058 --> 14:15.092
Apparently.

217
14:15.159 --> 14:17.661
Are you one of the hostesses sent here?

218
14:17.728 --> 14:18.896
Huh?

219
14:18.963 --> 14:23.934
You can go home. It's boring anyway. Get your tip from the guard outside.

220
14:24.768 --> 14:26.704
Heiresses like her usually have one weakness.

221
14:26.770 --> 14:28.572
Twisted loneliness.

222
14:28.639 --> 14:33.610
I came here to drink. What do you want to drink?

223
14:33.677 --> 14:34.778
Something expensive?

224
14:35.646 --> 14:37.448
Same thing as me? I'll treat you.

225
14:38.015 --> 14:39.450
If you're free, join me.

226
14:40.818 --> 14:42.586
Another bottle, two glasses.

227
14:42.653 --> 14:43.687
Yes, ma'am.

228
14:45.422 --> 14:46.623
You know the price?

229
14:47.491 --> 14:49.293
I'm rich, so it's fine.

230
14:49.360 --> 14:52.730
I'm a great thief.

231
14:52.796 --> 14:53.764
Huh?

232
14:59.503 --> 15:03.107
I'm Yayoi "Lupin" Kisaragi!

233
15:09.013 --> 15:11.815
Lupin? Which generation? The Fourth?

234
15:11.882 --> 15:14.351
-I'm the First. -So you're a reboot!

235
15:16.253 --> 15:20.591
Let's drink outside. The weather is nice. The night wind feels good, you know.

236
15:21.125 --> 15:24.194
-I can't. I have watchers. -Watchers?

237
15:24.828 --> 15:28.265
I'm a bad woman, so bad people watch me.

238
15:29.800 --> 15:33.404
-Yakuza? -Yes, my yakuza guardians.

239
15:35.305 --> 15:39.176
I'm a girl raised in a box, so I play inside the box.

240
15:39.843 --> 15:41.812
In that case…

241
15:42.880 --> 15:45.649
Lupin will steal you away.

242
15:53.891 --> 15:55.759
Ms. Miyabi has collapsed!

243
16:00.364 --> 16:03.300
-Wow… -Come on!

244
16:33.497 --> 16:34.731
YAYOI KISARAGI

245
16:35.532 --> 16:36.967
BEST BUDS

246
16:39.536 --> 16:40.704
Huh?

247
16:44.908 --> 16:46.577
Miyabi Kobayakawa?

248
16:47.811 --> 16:49.513
Local assembly members of the Kokuji Party

249
16:49.580 --> 16:53.784
were found to have avoided paying national health insurance premiums.

250
16:53.851 --> 16:55.853
They became nominal board members

251
16:55.919 --> 16:59.022
of an empty general incorporated association

252
16:59.089 --> 17:01.758
and set extremely low pay,

253
17:01.825 --> 17:03.927
keeping premiums of over one million yen

254
17:03.994 --> 17:06.363
down to a few tens of thousands.

255
17:06.430 --> 17:07.865
About this problem,

256
17:07.931 --> 17:09.700
Vice President Kobayakawa said…

257
17:09.766 --> 17:15.706
You say the party did bad things as an organization,

258
17:15.772 --> 17:17.574
but it's only a few people.

259
17:18.142 --> 17:20.511
It's an individual problem.

260
17:21.145 --> 17:23.313
The party doesn't need to apologize.

261
17:23.380 --> 17:26.250
Hours later, Secretary-General Iwakura said…

262
17:26.316 --> 17:29.953
We are truly sorry.

263
17:30.020 --> 17:33.824
The party apologized for 360 local assembly members

264
17:33.891 --> 17:37.060
who had avoided insurance premiums.

265
17:37.127 --> 17:39.630
This makes me look like a fool!

266
17:41.765 --> 17:43.467
The Prime Minister told me to…

267
17:44.468 --> 17:46.637
Well, he should have told me first.

268
17:47.204 --> 17:50.340
Before dissolving the House and calling the election,

269
17:50.407 --> 17:53.343
we should at least apologize for show.

270
17:53.410 --> 17:55.012
Will the full facts be revealed?

271
17:55.078 --> 17:56.413
We're investigating.

272
17:56.480 --> 17:58.282
Will you just punish four people?

273
17:58.849 --> 18:00.150
We're investigating.

274
18:00.217 --> 18:02.619
This was organized illegal activity, wasn't it?

275
18:03.253 --> 18:04.688
We're investigating.

276
18:04.755 --> 18:08.792
Will the members be expelled? Will you ask them to resign?

277
18:09.359 --> 18:10.794
We're investigating.

278
18:15.332 --> 18:16.466
On to the next news.

279
18:17.134 --> 18:19.102
She didn't even make a joke.

280
18:20.003 --> 18:21.672
She just accepted it.

281
18:22.806 --> 18:25.242
Her face and the silence said everything.

282
18:26.376 --> 18:29.146
-Hayate, enough. -Yes.

283
18:33.050 --> 18:34.685
Mr. Natsume, please sit.

284
18:34.751 --> 18:36.520
-You're a Diet member. -Yeah.

285
18:36.587 --> 18:38.855
-Don't mind us. -Thanks.

286
18:38.922 --> 18:40.490
-All right, then. -Go ahead.

287
18:41.058 --> 18:43.460
Hayate, you've been secretary for a year, right?

288
18:43.527 --> 18:47.965
Yes. I never thought I would have to run so soon.

289
18:48.031 --> 18:50.500
I should have watched my father's elections more closely.

290
18:50.567 --> 18:52.803
Don't worry. It's our home base.

291
18:53.537 --> 18:55.205
We'll give you a good strategist.

292
18:55.272 --> 18:57.808
-Thanks. -Natsume, will you look after him?

293
18:59.209 --> 19:00.077
You will, right?

294
19:00.143 --> 19:04.581
Hayate has no election experience. Natsume is in the Upper House,

295
19:05.148 --> 19:07.417
so your support would be reassuring.

296
19:08.285 --> 19:09.453
Right?

297
19:15.559 --> 19:16.994
I would be glad to help.

298
19:17.894 --> 19:18.829
Thank you.

299
19:20.030 --> 19:24.968
With our base, plus Hayate's fresh looks and popularity with women, we can't lose!

300
19:25.035 --> 19:27.337
Natsume, you have many female fans too.

301
19:28.405 --> 19:30.340
Then should us two form a unit?

302
19:30.407 --> 19:32.676
Hey now, don't get carried away.

303
19:40.651 --> 19:42.753
Getting on the daughter's good side

304
19:42.819 --> 19:45.055
won't get you into the Chief Cabinet Secretary's Office.

305
19:45.722 --> 19:48.925
I think she has better chances than me of becoming a Diet Member.

306
19:50.494 --> 19:54.498
I looked it up. In Nipponia, nearly 30% of Diet members are hereditary.

307
19:54.564 --> 19:57.067
In the Kokuji Party, over 40%.

308
19:57.134 --> 20:01.238
All of them are second, third, or fourth generation.

309
20:01.805 --> 20:05.075
Even so, I don't think Miyabi Kobayakawa can become a Diet Member.

310
20:07.978 --> 20:08.879
Yes?

311
20:09.980 --> 20:10.881
Hey, Miyabi.

312
20:12.449 --> 20:15.018
Why don't you try running for the Diet?

313
20:15.619 --> 20:17.421
-A Diet member? -Yes!

314
20:20.257 --> 20:23.827
My dad, my grandfather, my uncles,

315
20:23.894 --> 20:26.530
that uncle over there… It's full of those guys.

316
20:26.596 --> 20:29.032
Full of people like them. It's rotten.

317
20:29.099 --> 20:31.168
Soon my brother will rot too.

318
20:31.935 --> 20:33.737
Well, they may be rotten,

319
20:35.005 --> 20:37.207
but you should try joining them too!

320
20:37.274 --> 20:40.010
Be a Diet Member!

321
20:46.550 --> 20:49.019
HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES DISSOLUTION SPEECH

322
20:51.421 --> 20:54.291
Under Article 7 of the Nipponia Constitution,

323
20:54.858 --> 20:56.126
the House of Representatives

324
20:56.727 --> 20:58.095
is hereby dissolved.

325
20:58.662 --> 21:01.465
Banzai! Banzai!

326
21:06.737 --> 21:13.210
I can't believe they really dissolved it.

327
21:13.276 --> 21:15.479
Why would they?

328
21:16.446 --> 21:19.750
They still have their terms.

329
21:19.816 --> 21:25.789
Do the full term to the end! Ninety billion yen!

330
21:26.390 --> 21:32.929
If you have 90 billion to organize an election, put it into child support!

331
21:32.996 --> 21:37.200
I can't take this anymore!

332
21:39.569 --> 21:40.737
Mr. Natsume.

333
21:41.238 --> 21:43.140
I'm right behind you.

334
21:48.011 --> 21:51.748
I had a feeling you might be, but I couldn't stop myself.

335
21:53.116 --> 21:56.153
Good thing you noticed. Please continue.

336
22:07.831 --> 22:11.435
I heard that you ran from the bodyguards last night.

337
22:12.102 --> 22:14.104
Mr. Shiro was angry.

338
22:14.171 --> 22:16.339
I'll try not to run into him.

339
22:16.406 --> 22:18.642
He's quite busy with the election.

340
22:18.708 --> 22:20.310
Another election?

341
22:27.951 --> 22:28.952
What?

342
22:29.686 --> 22:32.255
You're serious? I'll fully support you.

343
22:33.757 --> 22:36.893
-What are you saying? -The video. Check your Winstagram.

344
22:37.461 --> 22:39.329
I've been waiting for this day.

345
22:39.396 --> 22:41.598
-Sorry, I'm hanging up. -Huh?

346
22:46.837 --> 22:49.673
I will become a Diet Member!

347
22:50.240 --> 22:51.074
What?

348
22:51.775 --> 22:53.543
I am running in this election!

349
22:54.144 --> 22:56.346
Everything is because of summer!

350
23:05.722 --> 23:07.090
YAYOI I GOT THE DOCUMENTS

351
23:12.929 --> 23:14.164
ELECTION APPLICATION FORM

352
23:14.231 --> 23:15.632
No way…

353
23:32.949 --> 23:34.050
She's fast.

354
23:38.788 --> 23:41.057
My Winsta. What was that? What is going on?

355
23:42.959 --> 23:43.994
You don't remember?

356
23:45.195 --> 23:46.162
What?

357
23:46.830 --> 23:47.664
Huh?!

358
23:47.731 --> 23:50.133
Have you ever thought of becoming a politician?

359
23:50.800 --> 23:52.903
Well, I have.

360
23:52.969 --> 23:54.137
What?

361
23:54.204 --> 23:56.940
I come from a political family. Of course I was interested.

362
23:57.007 --> 23:59.109
It was my dream in middle school.

363
23:59.175 --> 24:04.481
-Then… -They don't want female politicians.

364
24:04.548 --> 24:07.617
-There are many women now though. -Not many.

365
24:08.718 --> 24:11.888
Women are only 14% of the House of Representatives.

366
24:11.955 --> 24:17.227
Out of 180 countries, we rank 140th for the share of women.

367
24:17.294 --> 24:18.128
Really.

368
24:18.194 --> 24:20.764
See? They don't want us.

369
24:20.830 --> 24:23.500
-I want you. -To steal the money for her.

370
24:23.567 --> 24:25.535
-What did you say? -Miyabi.

371
24:26.202 --> 24:28.972
Life is short. Stand up, young lady!

372
24:29.039 --> 24:31.841
-It's "Fall in love, young lady." -This is no time for love!

373
24:31.908 --> 24:35.712
We will live. We'll survive in this Nipponia.

374
24:35.779 --> 24:38.315
-Survive, young lady? -Shout out loud, young lady!

375
24:38.381 --> 24:39.616
What should I shout?

376
24:39.683 --> 24:42.085
"I will become a Diet member!"

377
24:42.152 --> 24:43.720
-Huh? -Here!

378
24:43.787 --> 24:45.789
-Huh? -Repeat! Okay!

379
24:47.857 --> 24:50.794
I will become a Diet member!

380
24:52.295 --> 24:54.164
I am running in this election!

381
24:54.230 --> 24:57.834
Everything is because of summer!

382
25:02.072 --> 25:05.241
Perfect. That was a nice shout.

383
25:05.308 --> 25:08.845
-You two are just drunk. -Saying it out loud is important.

384
25:08.912 --> 25:11.815
So we won't forget it tomorrow. Let's start here.

385
25:11.881 --> 25:15.485
-Let's post this on my Winsta. -What?

386
25:16.119 --> 25:18.989
What? Wait! Don't touch social media when you're drunk.

387
25:19.055 --> 25:20.957
I'm not drunk.

388
25:22.726 --> 25:25.128
Yay! It's summer's fault!

389
25:26.496 --> 25:28.698
It's summer's fault. It's summer's fault.

390
25:30.867 --> 25:34.037
-It's fine. Why not do it for real? -No, never.

391
25:34.804 --> 25:38.508
I work as a consultant. It's my first election, but I can help.

392
25:38.575 --> 25:41.511
-Wait… -You posted it on Winsta.

393
25:41.578 --> 25:43.013
I deleted it.

394
25:43.079 --> 25:44.748
Don't you know deleting things makes it spread?

395
25:44.814 --> 25:46.816
No one will take it seriously.

396
25:47.550 --> 25:50.920
"That silly girl is saying silly things again." They'll laugh at me.

397
25:51.788 --> 25:53.256
That's not true…

398
25:53.323 --> 25:54.724
It is like that for me.

399
25:55.492 --> 25:57.260
It has always been like that.

400
25:57.827 --> 25:58.662
Jeez.

401
25:59.496 --> 26:02.032
It's better I don't try anything.

402
26:06.469 --> 26:10.106
My childhood dream was to be a thief.

403
26:11.041 --> 26:13.410
A great thief who travels the world.

404
26:14.244 --> 26:15.145
There it is.

405
26:15.845 --> 26:18.815
Yep. People laughed at me too, like that.

406
26:21.084 --> 26:22.819
But I was serious.

407
26:26.256 --> 26:27.991
I wanted to become a great thief

408
26:28.892 --> 26:30.627
and give money to everyone.

409
26:31.895 --> 26:33.697
So that the people I love

410
26:33.763 --> 26:36.933
would live life with a little more ease.

411
26:39.869 --> 26:41.037
So they could live

412
26:41.838 --> 26:42.939
happily.

413
26:44.307 --> 26:47.610
So they could feel glad to be alive.

414
26:59.289 --> 27:00.557
What I said last night,

415
27:01.257 --> 27:02.759
I meant that.

416
27:05.261 --> 27:06.463
I will

417
27:07.564 --> 27:08.832
steal you.

418
27:13.169 --> 27:14.904
Away from the cramped box

419
27:15.872 --> 27:17.640
that confines you.

420
27:22.946 --> 27:24.114
Do you want to get out?

421
27:25.148 --> 27:26.116
Or not?

422
27:29.119 --> 27:30.220
What do you want?

423
27:38.661 --> 27:39.763
What?

424
27:39.829 --> 27:41.898
Miyabi is running.

425
27:42.532 --> 27:43.733
In the general election.

426
27:43.800 --> 27:45.135
ELECTION APPLICATION FORM

427
27:47.303 --> 27:48.638
You'll help, right?

428
27:49.539 --> 27:50.607
Why me?

429
27:50.673 --> 27:54.210
You are that informant who is savvy about politics, right?

430
27:56.513 --> 27:58.181
Together, we can steal…

431
27:59.115 --> 28:00.517
those politicians' money.

432
28:08.158 --> 28:09.859
Stealing politics…

433
28:11.394 --> 28:13.296
That could be fun.

434
28:18.067 --> 28:20.436
My name is Inui.

435
28:34.217 --> 28:36.286
NIPPONIA ELECTION CANDIDATES SURVEY

436
28:36.352 --> 28:39.622
Tanaka, Miyamoto,

437
28:40.690 --> 28:42.025
and Hayate…

438
28:42.091 --> 28:45.195
Let's put them on the priority list.

439
28:45.962 --> 28:48.731
You said we would win easily.

440
28:50.066 --> 28:54.103
If Mr. Shiro's son happens to lose, it will be a disaster.

441
28:55.638 --> 28:57.640
Who do you propose we cut?

442
28:59.075 --> 29:02.011
-Natsume… -If you add people, you have to cut.

443
29:03.213 --> 29:06.282
The headwind against us is blowing hard.

444
29:06.349 --> 29:09.752
-We can't lose a single seat now. -With all due respect…

445
29:10.520 --> 29:12.255
We are over budget.

446
29:13.256 --> 29:15.658
You can't keep acting like a bureaucrat.

447
29:17.160 --> 29:19.362
If we lose this election, everything is meaningless.

448
29:20.296 --> 29:21.297
We are…

449
29:23.800 --> 29:24.934
over budget.

450
29:29.906 --> 29:33.243
Well, let's respect our Finance Director.

451
29:34.344 --> 29:36.145
It would be sad to hurt his motivation.

452
29:36.980 --> 29:38.147
Oh, right.

453
29:39.215 --> 29:41.251
Let's take it out of that safe.

454
29:41.885 --> 29:43.987
I'll tell my younger brother.

455
29:47.323 --> 29:50.226
-Call the Cabinet Secretary for support. -Roger.

456
29:51.194 --> 29:52.662
Starting next week,

457
29:52.729 --> 29:54.964
things will get busy.

458
29:57.667 --> 29:59.802
What? Here?

459
29:59.869 --> 30:01.204
It's a hideout.

460
30:02.438 --> 30:03.439
ORIENT HALL

461
30:03.506 --> 30:07.510
Inui has supported many politicians. He's amazing.

462
30:07.577 --> 30:13.149
Like Shin Sakuma, or Yoshiaki Ishizuka. Inui was behind all of their successes.

463
30:13.216 --> 30:17.720
But none of them will say they know Inui.

464
30:17.787 --> 30:20.089
After all, that remains a secret.

465
30:20.757 --> 30:22.859
Don't tell anyone about Inui.

466
30:22.926 --> 30:24.093
That's the condition.

467
30:24.694 --> 30:25.528
Understood.

468
30:26.396 --> 30:29.098
Well, he is not…

469
30:29.666 --> 30:31.301
a shady person at all.

470
30:31.367 --> 30:34.470
He's just an ordinary old man. Don't worry.

471
30:35.238 --> 30:39.208
Oh, welcome! Come on!

472
30:41.244 --> 30:42.812
See? Don't worry.

473
30:46.916 --> 30:49.452
-Did you write it? -Yes.

474
30:55.792 --> 30:56.993
Excuse me.

475
31:01.898 --> 31:04.968
Mr. Inui, you're an election pro, right?

476
31:05.034 --> 31:05.835
What?

477
31:06.869 --> 31:07.704
Yeah.

478
31:08.338 --> 31:11.274
I am basically an information broker who knows politics.

479
31:12.675 --> 31:13.576
And?

480
31:13.643 --> 31:16.212
-I know elections too. -Okay.

481
31:18.414 --> 31:20.783
Do you think I can win?

482
31:21.417 --> 31:24.554
I'm from a political family, but I have nothing.

483
31:24.620 --> 31:26.656
I'm 29 and unemployed.

484
31:26.723 --> 31:27.857
That's hard.

485
31:29.525 --> 31:34.030
A naive, rich girl with no backing sweeping up votes?

486
31:34.097 --> 31:35.665
The world isn't a fairy tale.

487
31:37.066 --> 31:37.900
However…

488
31:38.868 --> 31:40.236
There's a way.

489
31:57.253 --> 32:00.156
-Normally I leave it to my secretary. -Thank you.

490
32:00.790 --> 32:02.291
All experience is good.

491
32:02.925 --> 32:07.296
People from political families like me are always called out of touch.

492
32:08.965 --> 32:11.167
-Sorry to make you join me. -It's fine.

493
32:12.168 --> 32:13.403
Oh no!

494
32:15.204 --> 32:16.205
Miyabi?

495
32:17.974 --> 32:19.876
Miyabi? What are you doing?!

496
32:19.942 --> 32:22.545
Oh, wrong person. Excuse me.

497
32:24.414 --> 32:25.882
-Excuse me. -Excuse me.

498
32:26.682 --> 32:27.650
Excuse me.

499
32:33.356 --> 32:34.991
You're running for election?

500
32:35.625 --> 32:36.559
You?

501
32:42.565 --> 32:45.668
-Is that the shape of Chiba District 2? -Huh?

502
32:46.502 --> 32:48.771
District 2 is my father's electoral zone. Our home is there.

503
32:48.838 --> 32:51.140
-You have a house outside Tokyo? -Yeah.

504
32:51.741 --> 32:55.111
No one lives in it now, but our residence is still registered there.

505
32:55.178 --> 32:57.780
If we register in Tokyo, people will be upset.

506
32:57.847 --> 33:01.751
That's the base of the Kobayakawa kingdom.

507
33:01.818 --> 33:02.685
DISTRICT 2

508
33:02.752 --> 33:04.287
Do you know the vote-value gap?

509
33:05.855 --> 33:09.125
The number of residents differs by district.

510
33:09.826 --> 33:11.794
Because of population changes,

511
33:11.861 --> 33:14.163
the value of one vote differs by region.

512
33:14.230 --> 33:15.031
Correct.

513
33:15.598 --> 33:20.536
To correct this inequality, which relates to Article 14 of the Constitution,

514
33:20.603 --> 33:24.040
districts are redrawn regularly based on the census.

515
33:24.107 --> 33:26.242
This time was no exception.

516
33:27.076 --> 33:29.245
So, a new district was created.

517
33:32.448 --> 33:36.719
District 17. The eldest Kobayakawa son, Hayate, will run here.

518
33:37.920 --> 33:40.590
Father in District 2, Hayate in District 17.

519
33:40.656 --> 33:43.259
The plan is for them to win both.

520
33:44.460 --> 33:46.129
We'll put the daughter

521
33:46.963 --> 33:48.564
of the Kobayakawa family in District 17.

522
33:48.631 --> 33:49.499
What?

523
33:54.604 --> 33:55.972
Chiba District 17.

524
33:56.038 --> 33:58.674
Huh? The same as me?

525
34:00.076 --> 34:03.012
Does Mr. Shiro know about this?

526
34:07.650 --> 34:09.652
I don't think he'll allow it.

527
34:09.719 --> 34:15.291
Running is a citizen's right. Don't you know it, Mr. Masakado Natsume?

528
34:16.259 --> 34:20.463
Masakado Natsume, 45. Upper House member of the Kokuji Party.

529
34:20.530 --> 34:21.998
A former Finance Ministry official.

530
34:22.064 --> 34:24.500
In his second term since entering politics.

531
34:24.567 --> 34:26.369
Oh, Mr. Natsume!

532
34:26.969 --> 34:28.404
-Mr. Natsume! -Mr. Natsume!

533
34:28.471 --> 34:30.706
His serious-looking attractiveness gained him many fans.

534
34:32.542 --> 34:34.443
Politicians aren't idols.

535
34:35.177 --> 34:37.380
NATSUME I TRUST IN YOU

536
34:37.446 --> 34:40.783
He used to belong to no faction.

537
34:40.850 --> 34:42.685
But after factions broke up two years ago,

538
34:42.752 --> 34:45.755
he got close to the leaders of the old Kobayakawa faction.

539
34:45.821 --> 34:47.690
He was chosen as Finance Director.

540
34:47.757 --> 34:50.593
Meaning, he's the party's treasurer.

541
34:51.160 --> 34:54.597
So he's close to the Cabinet secret funds.

542
34:55.765 --> 34:59.435
As for his weakness, there are rumors about his relationships.

543
35:01.070 --> 35:04.173
He rarely refuses a date, but…

544
35:04.240 --> 35:05.708
This is delicious.

545
35:07.243 --> 35:08.878
Is it?

546
35:11.080 --> 35:15.851
My mother's chicken-and-egg rice bowl is much better.

547
35:18.387 --> 35:21.057
As a total mama's boy, he gets dumped right away.

548
35:21.757 --> 35:25.461
But some suspect he behaves like that on purpose.

549
35:25.528 --> 35:26.829
The truth is unknown.

550
35:27.730 --> 35:31.000
At least, he's the type who does not act coldly toward women.

551
35:33.302 --> 35:36.839
-Who are you? -I'm Yayoi. Miyabi's friend.

552
35:36.906 --> 35:39.141
What kind of friend?

553
35:39.208 --> 35:40.409
Are you perhaps…

554
35:41.277 --> 35:42.912
interested in me?

555
35:44.080 --> 35:45.014
Yes, I am.

556
35:47.016 --> 35:50.419
Oh, I'm happy.

557
36:09.639 --> 36:10.473
Sir!

558
36:11.173 --> 36:12.174
Sir!

559
36:12.241 --> 36:14.110
You're so noisy.

560
36:14.176 --> 36:15.745
Miyabi is running!

561
36:16.312 --> 36:17.380
Which horse is that?

562
36:18.314 --> 36:20.583
I'm talking about your daughter!

563
36:22.084 --> 36:24.620
She applied for screening at party headquarters.

564
36:25.788 --> 36:28.591
She'll run in Chiba District 17.

565
36:33.696 --> 36:35.531
No matter what you've done,

566
36:36.098 --> 36:38.934
even when you troubled our family, I always forgave you.

567
36:39.001 --> 36:40.202
What is your complaint?

568
36:41.203 --> 36:43.339
Causing trouble for your brother…

569
36:44.674 --> 36:46.609
Is it fun for you? Huh?

570
36:48.077 --> 36:49.779
Is someone tricking you?

571
36:50.346 --> 36:54.917
-Did some opposition party tempt you? -No. I'm independent.

572
36:54.984 --> 36:56.152
Miyabi.

573
36:56.218 --> 36:58.788
We are a special family.

574
37:00.356 --> 37:02.158
A priceless, beautiful,

575
37:02.925 --> 37:04.260
red diamond.

576
37:05.161 --> 37:08.764
Many people want to get their hands on such a jewel.

577
37:08.831 --> 37:11.067
I've told you since you were small.

578
37:11.901 --> 37:13.402
Don't let yourself get used.

579
37:14.704 --> 37:17.273
Become someone who uses people.

580
37:20.409 --> 37:21.811
What about you, brother?

581
37:22.378 --> 37:24.447
Aren't you being used by Dad?

582
37:25.314 --> 37:28.084
By the family pressure to become a politician?

583
37:28.150 --> 37:30.886
You used to say you wanted to create games.

584
37:32.021 --> 37:33.089
I was a kid.

585
37:33.155 --> 37:35.925
Then you joined our uncle's construction firm.

586
37:35.991 --> 37:37.593
Because Dad told you to.

587
37:37.660 --> 37:39.729
Then you quit to become his secretary.

588
37:39.795 --> 37:42.631
And now you're running. Because Dad said so, right?

589
37:43.699 --> 37:47.370
What will you do as a politician, brother? What do you want to do?

590
37:52.475 --> 37:53.542
Well…

591
37:55.111 --> 37:58.114
-I will influence the country… -How?

592
37:58.948 --> 38:00.850
Then what do you want to do?

593
38:08.057 --> 38:09.859
If I become a politician,

594
38:09.925 --> 38:11.927
I'll end the inheritance of seats.

595
38:14.597 --> 38:16.365
I'll reform the election system.

596
38:17.867 --> 38:18.768
What?

597
38:19.668 --> 38:21.070
How foolish.

598
38:38.220 --> 38:39.555
What are you doing?

599
38:40.689 --> 38:43.359
I need cash.

600
38:43.426 --> 38:47.062
-You can't do that. -No one will know if we stay quiet.

601
38:48.831 --> 38:51.000
-Sir! -Leave her alone.

602
38:51.967 --> 38:53.369
She will learn soon enough.

603
38:56.372 --> 38:59.508
Real politics aren't like a simulation game.

604
39:01.177 --> 39:04.113
HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES

605
39:04.980 --> 39:06.148
Mr. Natsume.

606
39:07.883 --> 39:09.752
Tell me about District 17.

607
39:09.819 --> 39:12.788
Hmm, I can't say anything.

608
39:12.855 --> 39:14.123
Don't be like that.

609
39:15.624 --> 39:16.759
I'll just say this.

610
39:17.660 --> 39:20.496
Miyabi can run if she wants, but she can't win.

611
39:30.105 --> 39:30.973
Excuse me.

612
39:31.540 --> 39:34.477
CHIEF CABINET SECRETARY OFFICE

613
39:35.578 --> 39:36.545
Yes.

614
39:36.612 --> 39:39.548
SECRETARY MATSUKICHI TAKENOKOSHI

615
39:41.650 --> 39:44.086
REQUESTED THE BELOW SUM FOR 8 REWARD PAYMENTS

616
39:44.153 --> 39:46.589
100 MILLION YEN

617
39:47.356 --> 39:49.058
-Take care of it. -Yes.

618
40:07.343 --> 40:10.946
In the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office, there is a big safe.

619
40:13.182 --> 40:15.484
It's full of money.

620
40:18.087 --> 40:21.290
It's stuffed with bundles of cash.

621
40:22.925 --> 40:25.361
It's the Cabinet's secret stash.

622
40:25.427 --> 40:28.797
Its official name is the Cabinet Secretariat Reward Funds.

623
40:28.864 --> 40:33.302
It's used to buy top-secret info, both at home and abroad.

624
40:33.369 --> 40:36.171
So no receipts are needed,

625
40:37.072 --> 40:40.743
and they don't have to report how it was used.

626
40:41.477 --> 40:46.048
So they exploit it and use the nation's money for their own party!

627
40:46.115 --> 40:48.083
The nation's money!

628
40:48.684 --> 40:53.322
It all comes from taxes. The people's sweat and blood!

629
40:53.389 --> 40:56.191
Is that even okay?

630
40:56.258 --> 40:58.928
The system is broken!

631
40:59.962 --> 41:02.965
Elections are about base, signboard, and bag.

632
41:03.032 --> 41:05.734
Signboard is how much fame you got. The bag is money.

633
41:05.801 --> 41:07.136
Campaign funds.

634
41:08.003 --> 41:11.840
Public support is great and all, but you need cash too.

635
41:12.975 --> 41:16.178
First, you must set up a support group, or no money moves.

636
41:16.245 --> 41:18.681
Deposit is three million.

637
41:18.747 --> 41:22.284
You need three million yen just to run? How expensive!

638
41:22.351 --> 41:25.688
It's not just three million. Everything costs money.

639
41:25.754 --> 41:29.992
Office rent, staff pay, campaign car, signs and banners,

640
41:30.059 --> 41:33.596
social media, online ads, flyers and newspaper ads,

641
41:33.662 --> 41:36.098
team jackets, lunches, expenses and extras.

642
41:36.165 --> 41:37.600
About 20 million in total!

643
41:40.135 --> 41:43.105
The more money, the higher the chance of winning.

644
41:43.172 --> 41:46.642
Even before the start date, the battle has already begun.

645
41:48.611 --> 41:49.778
Let me hear it.

646
41:53.616 --> 41:55.317
This is our seasonal greeting.

647
41:56.719 --> 41:58.854
Our seasonal greeting.

648
41:59.788 --> 42:01.557
Our seasonal greeting.

649
42:02.658 --> 42:05.227
Our seasonal greeting.

650
42:05.294 --> 42:07.463
Thank you very much.

651
42:16.605 --> 42:17.473
He's here.

652
42:17.539 --> 42:21.543
-Mr. Hayate, look over here! -Smile, please!

653
42:21.610 --> 42:23.245
That's Miyabi, his sister!

654
42:25.614 --> 42:28.350
Wow. You're like a celebrity.

655
42:28.417 --> 42:29.752
My parents are.

656
42:36.158 --> 42:37.793
-Thank you. -Yes.

657
42:37.860 --> 42:39.094
I'll check it.

658
42:41.230 --> 42:42.498
Excuse me…

659
42:43.499 --> 42:45.834
Oh, me? I'm Miyabi's friend.

660
42:48.103 --> 42:49.505
Another "friend."

661
42:50.339 --> 42:51.507
One more poster.

662
42:51.573 --> 42:53.509
This should be it.

663
42:54.376 --> 42:55.744
-Here? -Okay.

664
42:58.147 --> 43:00.849
-Let's call it a day. Thank you. -Thank you.

665
43:09.725 --> 43:13.462
-Who's this? -Miyabi's real friend, Kaoru Sera.

666
43:14.563 --> 43:15.864
Did you tell them you're a thief?

667
43:15.931 --> 43:17.366
Of course not.

668
43:18.033 --> 43:22.004
My cover is a consultant who wants to have more female politicians.

669
43:22.071 --> 43:24.940
Miyabi thinks the thief talk is a joke.

670
43:26.008 --> 43:27.009
You're a sly woman.

671
43:27.076 --> 43:29.912
A sly great thief.

672
43:31.647 --> 43:33.749
The road to the Cabinet Secretary's safe…

673
43:34.650 --> 43:36.085
is still long.

674
43:38.987 --> 43:40.322
Until then,

675
43:42.491 --> 43:45.594
I'll take Nagatanicho's money.

676
43:48.764 --> 43:51.300
It's all treasure.

677
44:01.777 --> 44:04.379
Next episode! Chiba District 17, the battlefield of the election.

678
44:04.446 --> 44:08.851
Hayate, the thoroughbred from a good family, against the wild horse, Miyabi.

679
44:08.917 --> 44:10.686
Will the brother win, or the sister?

680
44:10.753 --> 44:14.256
A battle between siblings turns sacred elections into a hellish scene!

681
44:14.323 --> 44:16.825
-Don't say "puke." -You brought it up first.

682
44:16.892 --> 44:18.227
No, I didn't say "puke."

683
44:18.293 --> 44:19.328
You just did.

684
44:19.394 --> 44:21.897
Will Nipponia be okay? Hang in there, Nipponia.

685
44:21.964 --> 44:24.800
The great thief takes her first step, sneaking into the world!

686
44:24.867 --> 44:26.702
The game of deception begins!

687
44:26.769 --> 44:29.037
We should thank the great thief.

688
44:29.104 --> 44:30.005
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
